      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(agents): Swarm core — collector spawn, agents_wait, structured output, caps (gated)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw has no way to orchestrate many subagents deterministically — no awaitable spawn, no structured child output, no fan-out caps. This is the core lane of the Swarm program (#110325).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPer the frozen spec (`docs/plan/swarms.md`, lands with this PR): one canonical, harness-agnostic owner of spawn/complete/settle semantics that both the QuickJS code-mode surface and the Codex-harness projection build on. Fully gated behind new `tools.swarm` config (default **off**) — with the gate closed, the only behavior change is param rejection with a clear error.\n\n## User Impact\n\nGated (off by default). When `tools.swarm.enabled`:\n- `sessions_spawn` gains `collect` (waitable completion record instead of announce/steering), `outputSchema` (validated structured output via injected `structured_output` tool, one nudge retry, `schemaError` fallback), `fastMode`, `groupId`; child identity defaults to `tools.swarm.defaultAgentId` (validated against the existing target allowlist).\n- New `agents_wait` tool: first-completion race semantics, bounded timeout, idempotent re-reads, spawner-chain ownership.\n- Per-group FIFO scheduler enforcing `maxConcurrent` / `maxChildrenPerGroup` / `maxTotalPerGroup`; collector children run approvals-fail-closed (denials reported in results, no operator prompts).\n- Persistence: additive columns on existing registry/state stores — no schema-version bump. Gateway-protocol change is additive-optional fields only.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused suites green locally: swarm-config, swarm-scheduler, agents-wait-tool, structured-output-tool, swarm-tools integration, agent-request-preflight (`node scripts/run-vitest.mjs …`, 2 shards).\n- Post-rebase full proof on Blacksmith Testbox: run 29657155074 (incl. 88-test state-db suite for the schema-architecture reconciliation).\n- Autoreview round 1 (codex gpt-5.6-sol): two P2s — per-request O(n) registry scan and missing collector lifecycle hooks — both fixed (index-maintaining run map for O(1) collector lookup + `isSubagentSessionKey`-gated store fallback; `subagent_progress`/`subagent_spawned` emitted from the scheduler start callback). Round 2: one finding rejected as factually incorrect — `resolveReal` already maps only ENOENT to null and rethrows otherwise, so non-ENOENT realpath failures return `false` (subagent-registry-helpers.ts:189-216).\n- Follow-ups tracked in #110325: QuickJS `agents.run` surface (in flight), dots widget, event-driven wait (replacing the bounded 25ms in-memory poll), `agents.session`.\n",
        "branch": "feat/swarm-core-0717",
